{% set local_problem %}
<p>We've lived and worked in Hartselle long enough to know exactly how fast gutters fill up around here. The established neighborhoods downtown have mature trees that drop leaves by the truckload every fall. The properties outside town often have pine coverage that sheds needles constantly. Even the newer developments have enough tree coverage to keep gutters filling.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, the problems start quickly. Overflowing water runs down your siding, pools around your foundation, and eventually finds its way into places it shouldn't be. Morgan County's soil conditions mean that pooled water often stays pooled, creating conditions for foundation damage and basement moisture.</p>

<p>Many Hartselle homeowners try to handle gutter cleaning themselves, but it's time-consuming and potentially dangerous work. Climbing ladders, reaching across rooflines, dealing with decomposed debris — it's not a pleasant way to spend a Saturday. And for homes with steep roofs or multiple stories, DIY cleaning can be genuinely risky.</p>

<p>That's where we come in. We've been cleaning gutters for Hartselle neighbors for over 20 years. We're fast, we're thorough, and we're right here in town when you need us.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss — debris backs up in the downspout, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag developing problems before they become expensive repairs. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

